            "artifact": "campaigns\\evaluations\\366d41cb-aeb7-4a5c-bbb0-5216fbc99e43\\dynamics_probe.json",
            "instrument": "python_module",
            "label": "startup dynamics authority probe",
            "module": "robot_learning.lab.dynamics_probe"
          }
        ],
        "rationale": "The scientific model makes this the consequential startup distinction: action bounds and XML geometry do not establish whether the 20 ms held control interval, derived inertias, damping, joint limits, and direct motor authority permit rapid stable regulation. This deterministic probe uses the authoritative XML and records model quantities plus boundary-aligned saturated and pulse traces, so its outcomes can redirect the first learning method rather than merely restating structural assumptions. If responses are fast and settle with margin, policy learning and the omitted inner-radius exposure become the credible next bottleneck; if they saturate, ring, or approach limits, the first method must address dynamics-aware stabilization and branch/trajectory behavior. It is not an official evaluation."
      },
